      "id": "GDC-01",
      "chapter": "lifts",
      "anchor": "lifts-geometric-determinant-character",
      "title": "Where does the prescribed determinant come from?",
      "hypotheses": "An irreducible automorphic representation of positive rank m on the definite unitary group is given, together with the identification of coefficients. The local assertion is at a split spherical place.",
      "statement": "The central character twisted by the inverse t-th idèle norm gives a continuous Galois character with the required normalized Satake product, for t=m(m−1)/2. At a place over ℓ the local rank-one comparison gives crystallinity, its labelled jump and its Weil value at geometric degree −1.",
